"macOS gives every open app its own Dock icon, and only the Dock itself can leave one out. With System Integrity Protection (SIP) partly off, Dock Folders can do that from inside the Dock, so an open app shows only in its folder. SIP helps protect your Mac from malware; only turn it off if you’re comfortable with less of that protection." = "macOS 会为每个打开的 App 显示独立的程序坞图标，且只有程序坞自身可以隐藏这些图标。关闭部分系统完整性保护（SIP）后，Dock Folders 可从程序坞内部实现此操作，让打开的 App 仅在文件夹中显示。SIP 有助于保护 Mac 免受恶意软件侵害；关闭部分保护会降低安全性，请确认你能接受后再操作。";
